  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the interaction with NCI-H2405 through a series of molecular pathways involving the P2X purinoceptor 1 and [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is identified as a target of Mollicellin N, suggesting a potential pharmacological interaction. The pathway connects Mollicellin N to NCI-H2405 via a shared target, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which is a known modulator of P2X purinoceptors. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N may act through this compound to influence the cellular activity of NCI-H2405, potentially through receptor activation or downstream signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Mollicellin N could exert its effects on NCI-H2405, emphasizing the role of P2X purinoceptors in mediating this interaction.",
